### Step 1 – Use consistent colors and fonts

#### What I did in Power BI
- Applied a report theme via View → Themes.
- Customized the current theme:
  - Set one font family for the whole report.
  - Chose one main accent color and kept other colors neutral.
- Standardized visual formatting across pages:
  - Titles on all visuals with consistent font size and naming style.
  - Consistent axis/label font sizes.
  - Consistent number formatting (currency for sales, no decimals for counts).
- Standardized KPI cards:
  - Same title/value sizes, background and borders.
  - Aligned and evenly distributed cards.
- Cleaned layout:
  - Used gridlines and snap-to-grid.
  - Aligned visuals and kept spacing consistent.

#### What I learned
- Themes enforce a consistent visual style quickly.
- Consistent fonts and colors improve readability and professionalism.
- Aligning and spacing visuals makes the report feel like one cohesive app.

